    ":question/id": "82583355-6299-599e-bdc6-d65fa8aebd0a",
    ":question/problem": "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 2 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=x^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2 x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x &= 1\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &= - \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}+C \\\\ &= - \\cos{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"
