    ":question/id": "9f181c0b-4ade-5cfb-806e-89c254367d4c",
    ":question/problem": "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 8 x^{2} \\sec^{2}{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=x^{3},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3 x^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 8 x^{2} \\sec^{2}{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x &= \\frac{8}{3}\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &= \\frac{8 \\tan{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}+C \\\\ &= \\frac{8 \\tan{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"
